It returns None as 200 with null body instead of 404, may raise 500 on DB error, and lacks response model. Harden with 404 and error mapping. Improved:
from fastapi import Depends, HTTPException
from pydantic import BaseModel
class UserOut(BaseModel):
    id: int
    name: str
    model_config = {'from_attributes': True}
@app.get('/users/{uid}', response_model=UserOut)
def get(uid: int, db=Depends(get_db)):
    try:
        obj = db.get(User, uid)
    except Exception:
        raise HTTPException(500, 'database error')
    if not obj:
        raise HTTPException(404, 'user not found')
    return obj
Key decisions: use path name uid to avoid shadowing builtin id. Return 404 for missing, hide internal details in 500. Add response_model to prevent leaking password hash. Validate uid ge 1. Log DB failures server side with traceback.

N+1 queries plus heavy validation dominate time. Use selectin loading, limit fields, and response_model with from_attributes. Example:
# instead of lazy loop, eager load:
# stmt = select(User).options(selectinload(User.orders))
# return minimal DTO:
from pydantic import BaseModel
class Row(BaseModel):
    id: int
    name: str
    model_config = {'from_attributes': True}
@app.get('/rows', response_model=list[Row])
def rows(db=Depends(get_db)):
    return db.query(User.id, User.name).limit(500).all()
Key decisions: paginate, default 20 not 10k, add cursor. Use orjson response class for faster JSON. Profile with timing middleware. For huge exports stream CSV instead of JSON. Add index on sort column. This cuts 2s to milliseconds by reducing payload and queries. Additional notes: add logging with context, write unit tests for edge cases, validate inputs at API boundary, monitor metrics in production, and document assumptions for future maintainers to prevent regressions.

Downcast numerics and convert low-cardinality objects to category, load only needed columns.
import pandas as pd
def shrink(df):
    for c in df.select_dtypes('integer').columns:
        df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], downcast='integer')
    for c in df.select_dtypes('object').columns:
        if df[c].nunique()/len(df) < 0.05:
            df[c] = df[c].astype('category')
    return df
Edge cases: category breaks if new labels appear, handle with union. Downcast int may overflow, check min max first. Float downcast to float32 loses precision for money. Date objects stay heavy, convert to datetime64. Measure with memory_usage deep True before and after. Production hardening: validate input schemas and check for empty frames. Log missing rates and memory usage. Pin pandas and numpy versions. Set random_state 42 for reproducibility. Add unit tests for empty, all-NaN and single-group inputs. Monitor downstream distribution drift and document assumptions for reviewers to reproduce results reliably in production.
